## Notes on Arguments and Attributes

- `use_manifest_namespaces`: For Kubernetes only – respect namespaces in the manifest (default: `false`)
- `kubernetes_prune`: Sent as `DeployerOptions` on create and update (not for `helm_config` stacks)
- `kubernetes_force_apply`: Kubernetes only (`deployment_type = 1`), Portainer 3.0+: delete and recreate a resource whose immutable fields changed instead of failing the deployment (destroys the resource and everything tied to its identity).
- `pre_pull_image`: Defaults to `false`.
- `retry_deploy`: Whether to retry deploy if first attempt fails (default: `false`)
- `dryrun`: If true, validate but do not persist the Edge Stack (default: `false`)
- `repository_reference_name`: Defaults to `refs/heads/main`.
- `file_path_in_repository`: Defaults to `docker-compose.yml`.
- `git_repository_authentication`: Enable auth for Git repo (default: `false`)
- `repository_password_wo_version`: Forces recreation, like `repository_password`
- `stack_webhook`: Defaults to `false`.
- `update_interval`: Polling interval (enables GitOps polling, e.g. `30m`, `1h`)
- `force_update`: Whether to force redeploy (default: `false`)
- `pull_image`: When `true`, updates also send `RepullImageAndRedeploy`, which replaces the `RePullImage` flag Portainer deprecated in 2.36. Portainer's create endpoints (string, file, repository, Helm) have no re-pull field, so it is not sent when the stack is created, except as `AutoUpdate.ForcePullImage` of a GitOps repository stack; a new stack pulls its images on its first deployment anyway, and `pre_pull_image` pulls them before it. Until the first update Portainer reports `false`, and the configured `true` is kept.
- `repository_git_credential_id`: ID of the Git credentials to use (replaces username/password)
- `always_clone`: Defaults to `false`.

## Arguments by Deployment Method

### For String-based Edge Stack
Arguments: `stack_file_content`.

### For File-based Edge Stack
Arguments: `stack_file_path`, `pre_pull_image`, `retry_deploy`, `dryrun`.

### For Repository-based Edge Stack
Arguments: `repository_url`, `source_id`, `repository_reference_name`, `file_path_in_repository`, `git_repository_authentication`, `repository_username`, `repository_password`, `repository_password_wo`, `repository_password_wo_version`, `stack_webhook`, `update_interval`, `force_update`, `pull_image`, `relative_path`, `repository_git_credential_id`, `always_clone`, `per_device_configs_path`, `per_device_configs_match_type`, `per_device_configs_group_match_type`, `helm_config`, `stagger_config`.

### `helm_config` Block

> **Business Edition only.** The Helm repository endpoints do not exist in Portainer CE.

Setting this block selects the Helm repository deployment source, the same way `stack_file_content` selects the inline one. It is mutually exclusive with `stack_file_content`, `stack_file_path` and `repository_url`.

A Helm chart deploys to Kubernetes, so `deployment_type` has to be `1`.

Leaving `chart_version` unset means Portainer resolves the latest published version at apply time, so a later apply can move the stack to a newer chart without the configuration changing. Pin it where that matters.

The optional fields are left out of the request when empty, so an update never clears a chart setting that was configured outside Terraform.

### `stagger_config` Block

> **Business Edition only.** Community Edition ignores it. Only sent when the block is set: leaving it out keeps the stagger configuration Portainer has recorded. Read back only while the block is configured (an import does not bring it in).

Rolls an update of the stack out to its devices in batches. Sent on every create and update endpoint (string, file, repository and Helm stacks).

